# f1 = cut. The key is held below the length, the length is stored over, and the element is read. The store ends what the walk knows of the length: the read asks for itself.
# Fault injection, testing=IgnoreLengthStores: the walk assumes that the read is in bounds because of the test before the store.
# The code verifier walks back from an access to each piece of its bounds evidence that was read from the array.
# It rejects the code where the storage or the length of the same array is written on the path.
# OPTIONS: testing=IgnoreLengthStores
# DIAGNOSTIC: OpcodeNotInForm f1
# RUN: walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# CHECK-NOT: code f1:Body
